course: dictionary
lesson: 1395
title: A jug on the table
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you can see and touch, and a carafe is one of them. You do not need to own one to understand it. Read the words around it, because they give you clues. «The waiter placed a carafe of water on our table.» Waiters bring drinks to tables, and water is poured from a jug, so a carafe must be a kind of jug.
explain: Check your idea by swapping in a word you know. Put «jug» in place of «carafe»: «The waiter placed a jug of water on our table.» It still makes sense, so jug is a good meaning. A carafe is a special kind of jug, made of glass, with a narrow neck and no lid.
explain: Words from other languages work the same way. In France you may see «une carafe d'eau». The clue is eau, which means water, so «une carafe d'eau» means a jug of water. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A carafe is a glass jug with a narrow neck and no lid.
fact: A carafe is used for serving water or wine at the table.
fact: In French, «une carafe d'eau» means a jug of tap water, and in French restaurants it is free.
fact: In French, «de l'eau plate» is still water, and «de l'eau gazeuse» is sparkling water.
fact: In maths, a carafe may hold 1 litre, so you can work out how many glasses it fills.
exercise: What is a carafe? | A metal tin for soup | *A glass jug with a narrow neck and no lid | A small glass cup with a handle | A bottle with a cork in it
exercise: «The waiter placed a carafe of water on our table.» What would fit in place of carafe? | *A jug | A plate | A bed | A window
exercise: A carafe holds 1 litre. A glass holds a quarter of a litre. How many glasses fill the carafe? | 2 | 10 | 3 | *4
test: In French, «de l'eau plate» means? | Sea water | *Still water | Hot water | Sparkling water
test: In a French restaurant, «une carafe d'eau» is? | *Free tap water | Hot soup | Lemon juice | Bottled water that costs extra
exam: «The waiter poured water from the carafe into my glass.» What is the best clue that a carafe is a jug? | It is always full of wine | It is worn on the head | *Water is poured from it into a glass | It has four wheels
